WEBVTT

00:00.930 --> 00:03.920
<i>After punching their ticket to the Nationals,</i>

00:03.920 --> 00:08.520
<i>Tsubasa learns from Wakabayashi that Taro Misaki is currently in France.</i>

00:08.520 --> 00:11.070
<i>Upon hearing what his old friend is up to,</i>

00:11.070 --> 00:13.910
<i>Tsubasa finds himself even more fired up!</i>

00:13.910 --> 00:16.570
<i>Meanwhile, in hopes of getting more powerful,</i>

00:16.570 --> 00:22.040
<i>Kojiro has been undergoing some harsh training at his old coach Kira's place.</i>

00:24.340 --> 00:28.040
The tiger is back from his slumber now!

00:28.040 --> 00:30.420
<i>In order to respond to Kojiro's efforts,</i>

00:30.420 --> 00:34.900
<i>Tsubasa keeps working hard on perfecting his Drive Shot.</i>

00:35.800 --> 00:38.890
<i>And here we are, at the day of the National Tournament.</i>

00:38.890 --> 00:42.730
<i>After completing his training, Kojiro reunites with his team.</i>

00:42.730 --> 00:44.060
<i>However...</i>

00:45.260 --> 00:48.790
Hyuga, I won't allow you to play in this tournament.

00:50.070 --> 00:56.180
<i>The curtain falls on the Nationals with unexpected developments brewing!</i>

00:58.410 --> 01:01.200
<i>The first match draws the attention of every school.</i>

01:01.200 --> 01:05.040
<i>The opening game of the National Middle School Football Tournament</i>

01:05.040 --> 01:10.340
<i>will be between Nankatsu MS from Shizuoka Prefecture, and Azumaichi MS from Osaka.</i>

01:10.340 --> 01:12.550
<i>The game will start shortly.</i>

01:15.540 --> 01:19.270
<i>Nankatsu aims for their 3rd championship for the first time in their history,</i>

01:19.270 --> 01:24.100
<i>and are taking their first step towards that, with Tsubasa Ozora at the helm.</i>

01:24.100 --> 01:27.240
<i>Azumaichi MS beat last year's Osaka representative, Naniwa MS,</i>

01:27.240 --> 01:29.360
<i>and this is their first time in this tournament.</i>

01:29.360 --> 01:32.690
<i>Despite facing the reigning champions, they show no signs of panic.</i>

01:35.720 --> 01:39.490
<i>Azumaichi's center-back Soda is going to encounter them!</i>

01:39.490 --> 01:41.740
Don't you dare play so slow!

01:43.200 --> 01:44.700
Here! Take this!

01:44.700 --> 01:46.160
<i>He sends the ball ahead!</i>

01:46.160 --> 01:48.000
Like I'd let it pass!

01:48.000 --> 01:51.750
<i>Tsubasa is immediately there to cut it!</i>

01:52.180 --> 01:53.960
Nice one, Tsubasa!

01:53.960 --> 01:55.260
This bastard...

01:55.260 --> 01:59.720
<i>It's apparent that both aces are all fired up!</i>

02:04.220 --> 02:06.930
<i>Ai! Ai! Ai!</i>

02:04.220 --> 02:06.930
<i>Love! Love! Love!</i>

02:07.840 --> 02:10.510
<i>Ai! Ai! Ai!</i>

02:07.840 --> 02:10.510
<i>Love! Love! Love!</i>

02:11.430 --> 02:14.140
<i>Ai! Ai! Ai!</i>

02:11.430 --> 02:14.140
<i>Love! Love! Love!</i>

02:21.020 --> 02:23.860
<i>moeru you ni hitori demo</i>

02:21.020 --> 02:23.860
<i>I keep running, lying to myself</i>

02:23.860 --> 02:30.120
<i>ikiteyukeru to usobuite hashiritsudzukete</i>

02:23.860 --> 02:30.120
<i>that I can live alone, though the loneliness makes me burn</i>

02:30.120 --> 02:36.000
<i>unubore no morosa wo kimi wa shitteta na no ni</i>

02:30.120 --> 02:36.000
<i>You knew how fragile my self-conceit makes me</i>

02:36.000 --> 02:42.590
<i>kokoro made uchinomaresareta kono yoru ni</i>

02:36.000 --> 02:42.590
<i>In this night that even shattered my heart</i>

02:42.590 --> 02:46.590
<i>kimi no koe sagasu</i>

02:42.590 --> 02:46.590
<i>I hate how weak I am</i>

02:46.590 --> 02:51.100
<i>kono yowasa ga nikui yo</i>

02:46.590 --> 02:51.100
<i>yearning for your voice</i>

02:51.100 --> 02:56.640
<i>ima sugu torimodoshi ni ikanakya</i>

02:51.100 --> 02:56.640
<i>"I've got to get you back right now!"</i>

02:56.640 --> 02:58.230
<i>baka darou?</i>

02:56.640 --> 02:58.230
<i>I'm stupid, right?</i>

02:58.230 --> 02:59.440
<i>ai</i>

02:58.230 --> 02:59.440
<i>Love!</i>

02:59.440 --> 03:02.940
<i>kizudarake no ai wo shinjite</i>

02:59.440 --> 03:02.940
<i>Believing in my scarred love</i>

03:02.940 --> 03:12.830
<i>nagareochita namida sae mo tsuyosa e to kaete</i>

03:02.940 --> 03:12.830
<i>I will turn these shedded tears into strength</i>

03:12.830 --> 03:13.660
<i>ai</i>

03:12.830 --> 03:13.660
<i>Love!</i>

03:13.660 --> 03:17.460
<i>kizudarake no ai da to shite mo</i>

03:13.660 --> 03:17.460
<i>Even though it is a scarred love</i>

03:17.460 --> 03:21.460
<i>bokura no sekai wo tomoshiteru</i>

03:17.460 --> 03:21.460
<i>it lightens up our world</i>

03:21.460 --> 03:27.720
<i>kono ai mo ichido taritomo</i>

03:21.460 --> 03:27.720
<i>I will not let go of this love</i>

03:27.720 --> 03:30.510
<i>hanasanai</i>

03:27.720 --> 03:30.510
<i>for a single moment!</i>

03:32.100 --> 03:36.230
<b><b>EPISODE 35:
RAZOR POWER EXPLODES</b></b>

03:36.270 --> 03:37.380
<i>That's right.</i>

03:37.380 --> 03:41.070
<i>I can't think about taking this lightly while I'm aiming for our V3.</i>

03:41.640 --> 03:46.080
<i>No matter who we're playing against, I'll give my all in every single match!</i>

03:47.830 --> 03:49.350
Follow Tsubasa's lead!

03:49.350 --> 03:50.000
Yeah!

03:50.000 --> 03:52.040
<i>Soda is after him as well!</i>

03:52.040 --> 03:54.920
<i>I won't let you be in the spotlight this match!</i>

03:55.940 --> 03:58.140
He's keeping up with Tsubasa's speed!

03:58.140 --> 04:01.630
That guy wasn't all talk!

04:01.630 --> 04:02.470
He disappeared!

04:03.390 --> 04:05.190
Razor Tackle!

04:05.190 --> 04:06.080
Wha—

04:06.080 --> 04:14.400
<i>Soda changes sides to go to Tsubasa's blind spot and performs a powerful sliding tackle!</i>

04:14.770 --> 04:16.520
Did he say "Razor Tackle"?

04:16.520 --> 04:17.900
Man, that was one sharp tackle!

04:19.280 --> 04:20.990
Good! This is our chance!

04:21.900 --> 04:23.220
Go for it, guys!

04:23.220 --> 04:24.200
A fast attack!

04:24.200 --> 04:29.490
<i>While Nankatsu's offensive and defensive keystone Tsubasa is down, Azumaichi MS starts their attack!</i>

04:30.240 --> 04:31.620
I won't let you!

04:32.250 --> 04:33.500
Here!

04:33.500 --> 04:37.670
<i>Azumaichi MS are the first with a chance today!</i>

04:37.670 --> 04:38.250
God damn it!

04:38.670 --> 04:39.300
Here you go!

04:39.300 --> 04:42.090
<i>Ide is positioned in front of Nankatsu's goal.</i>

04:42.090 --> 04:44.430
<i>Onodera is waiting for him!</i>

04:45.260 --> 04:46.390
What?!

04:46.390 --> 04:47.640
All right!

04:47.640 --> 04:51.850
<i>Center-back Soda overlaps and is completely unmarked!</i>

04:52.850 --> 04:53.880
Don't let him shoot!

04:53.880 --> 04:55.480
Don't give him an angle!

04:56.580 --> 04:59.320
<i>You think this is enough to stop me?</i>

04:59.320 --> 05:02.820
<i>Let me show you with this one shot!</i>

05:06.820 --> 05:12.700
Go! Razor Shot!

05:12.700 --> 05:15.210
<i>Soda fires away!</i>

05:16.330 --> 05:17.330
Morisaki!

05:17.330 --> 05:18.080
You can catch it!

05:19.250 --> 05:20.670
<i>Morisaki reaches out!</i>

05:22.170 --> 05:22.840
<i>What?!</i>

05:24.840 --> 05:26.170
<i>Goal!</i>

05:26.170 --> 05:29.600
<i>The ball digs its way right into the upper right corner!</i>

05:29.600 --> 05:31.280
Damn right!

05:31.280 --> 05:34.100
<i>We've just seen Soda's Razor Shot!</i>

05:35.350 --> 05:36.100
What?

05:36.100 --> 05:38.100
Nankatsu gave up a goal first!

05:39.730 --> 05:44.740
<i>In the 5th minute of the first half, the reigning champions Nankatsu have conceded a goal!</i>

05:45.320 --> 05:48.240
<i>The goalscorer was the defender, Makoto Soda.</i>

05:48.240 --> 05:49.640
That's right.

05:49.640 --> 05:54.500
<i>That was Soda's Razor Shot, which we'd also seen at Osaka Tournament's final.</i>

05:54.500 --> 05:56.660
Makoto Soda...

05:56.660 --> 05:57.820
You morons!

05:57.820 --> 05:59.210
You've been too careless!

05:59.210 --> 06:03.170
<i>This National Middle School Football Tournament has taken quite the turn!</i>

06:03.170 --> 06:06.310
<i>In the opening game between Nankatsu and Azumaichi,</i>

06:06.310 --> 06:09.940
<i>the first to concede a goal are the reigning champions, Nankatsu.</i>

06:09.940 --> 06:14.220
<i>For those watching, the match has certainly become very interesting!</i>

06:14.220 --> 06:17.160
Guys, the match has just begun.

06:17.160 --> 06:19.350
Don't panic; let's calmly focus on our game!

06:19.350 --> 06:20.440
Yes!

06:20.440 --> 06:21.420
Morisaki!

06:21.420 --> 06:24.980
That guy seems to put a frightening amount of spins to his shots.

06:24.980 --> 06:26.490
Be careful!

06:26.490 --> 06:28.740
Okay, got it.

06:31.120 --> 06:34.370
Soda didn't take his time...

06:34.370 --> 06:36.620
—  BAY COAST STADIUM —

06:36.620 --> 06:38.620
One, two, three, four!

06:38.620 --> 06:40.130
Hey, look at that.

06:40.130 --> 06:41.790
Hyuga is sitting on the bench.

06:41.790 --> 06:45.260
He's all beaten up, but he looks... tougher than before.

06:45.260 --> 06:49.380
Hasn't he been secretly training since the end of the Tokyo Tournament?

06:49.380 --> 06:52.970
So all that about "Hyuga's disappearance" was just blowing smoke?

06:53.860 --> 06:55.220
Here's Coach Kitazume!

06:55.220 --> 06:56.770
Coach Kitazume!

06:56.770 --> 06:59.500
Can we ask you about Hyuga?

06:59.500 --> 07:03.860
Was him going "missing" some sort of special secret training?

07:03.860 --> 07:06.740
Secret training? I've heard nothing about that.

07:06.740 --> 07:09.450
Everything about Hyuga gets a "no comment" from me.

07:09.450 --> 07:11.910
Oh, please don't hide it.

07:11.910 --> 07:13.910
He's done some really hard training, right?

07:13.910 --> 07:15.030
Enough!

07:15.030 --> 07:17.330
The only thing I can say right now is that

07:17.330 --> 07:20.920
I won't let Hyuga play in this tournament!

07:20.920 --> 07:21.920
Wha—

07:21.920 --> 07:23.500
Coach...

07:28.340 --> 07:30.760
<i>Nankatsu has stumbled right from the start!</i>

07:30.760 --> 07:34.470
<i>As usual, the one to get them back on their feet is Tsubasa Ozora!</i>

07:34.470 --> 07:36.470
We're counting on you, Tsubasa!

07:39.140 --> 07:42.280
After scoring that one goal, all I have to do is mark you.

07:42.280 --> 07:44.060
If I do that, this game's as good as ours.

07:46.820 --> 07:47.980
<i>Damn him!</i>

07:49.120 --> 07:49.740
Crap!

07:49.740 --> 07:54.370
<i>Despite Soda marking closely, Tsubasa manages to pass it away.</i>

07:54.370 --> 07:57.920
<i>Any team would thoroughly mark Tsubasa.</i>

07:57.920 --> 08:01.750
<i>The important part is how Tsubasa and his teammates handle it.</i>

08:01.750 --> 08:02.810
Let's go!

08:02.810 --> 08:05.540
Let's show them Nankatsu isn't just about Tsubasa.

08:05.540 --> 08:06.710
All right!

08:06.710 --> 08:09.630
<i>Nankatsu plans to doggedly break through the middle!</i>

08:09.630 --> 08:11.510
Like hell we'd let you!

08:11.510 --> 08:13.970
<i>However, Azumaichi's defense is also strong!</i>

08:16.700 --> 08:17.100
<i>Damn it!</i>

08:17.100 --> 08:19.770
<i>So he'll be marking me even when I dont have the ball.</i>

08:19.770 --> 08:20.930
<i>You're damn right.</i>

08:20.930 --> 08:23.270
<i>I'll follow you to the depths of hell. </i>

08:23.850 --> 08:26.420
If it's come to this, let's see who's got better stamina!

08:26.420 --> 08:28.060
I'll break away from your marking!

08:28.060 --> 08:31.190
Hmph! You can't outrun me!

08:31.190 --> 08:34.700
<i>Nankatsu continues their attack without Tsubasa.</i>

08:34.700 --> 08:38.030
<i>Azumaichi's Soda's obstinate marking is working.</i>

08:38.030 --> 08:41.080
<i>That's Soda for you. You're as stubborn as a snake.</i>

08:41.080 --> 08:43.250
<i>It's been 10 minutes since the start of the match.</i>

08:43.250 --> 08:44.250
Tsubasa!

08:45.000 --> 08:48.340
<i>Izawa's pass successfully makes its way to Tsubasa.</i>

08:48.340 --> 08:49.400
<i>He's the real deal.</i>

08:49.400 --> 08:52.760
<i>He's the first player to give this a hard time with his man-marking.</i>

08:52.760 --> 08:54.980
<i>You're as good as they say, Tsubasa Ozora.</i>

08:54.980 --> 08:58.640
<i>I managed to use a Razor Tackle on him earlier, but he won't give me another chance.</i>

08:58.640 --> 09:02.620
That center-back's defense skills on the wings is pretty good.

09:02.620 --> 09:05.810
That's #7... Makoto Soda.

09:05.810 --> 09:11.530
He's good at marking others, and he can play anywhere in a defensive position.

09:12.280 --> 09:14.530
I see...

09:14.530 --> 09:17.540
Tsubasa! You can shake a guy like him off yourself!

09:17.540 --> 09:19.620
We'll run to the front of the goal for you!

09:19.620 --> 09:21.410
Just give us a cross!

09:21.410 --> 09:22.660
Well, I can't have that!

09:22.660 --> 09:24.250
I will!

09:28.040 --> 09:29.660
<i>He stopped him!</i>

09:29.660 --> 09:31.960
<i>Soda tackles him from behind.</i>

09:31.960 --> 09:32.800
What?!

09:34.500 --> 09:36.130
<i>That's a foul!</i>

09:36.130 --> 09:38.680
That bastard! He did that on purpose!

09:39.380 --> 09:40.640
<i>Yellow card!</i>

09:40.640 --> 09:45.750
<i>If Soda gets another yellow card, he'll be put out of the game.</i>

09:45.750 --> 09:49.100
<i>When I mark someone, I stop him no matter the cost.</i>

09:49.100 --> 09:51.680
<i>Even if I have to resort to a foul or two.</i>

09:52.360 --> 09:55.660
<i>Azumaichi MS fights bravely in their first national tournament.</i>

09:55.660 --> 09:58.700
<i>It seems not giving Tsubasa room to direct the game is working well.</i>

09:58.700 --> 10:00.180
Get a hold of yourselves!

10:00.180 --> 10:02.080
Just like you did against us in the finals,

10:02.080 --> 10:04.580
show them you can play, even without Tsubasa!

10:04.580 --> 10:05.850
Damn it!

10:05.850 --> 10:07.930
If we can't create a chance with Tsubasa...

10:07.930 --> 10:09.540
we'll make one ourselves!

10:09.540 --> 10:11.640
We're counting on you, Shutetsu Trio!

10:11.640 --> 10:15.130
<i>The heart of Nankatsu's offense Izawa, Taki and Kisugi</i>

10:15.130 --> 10:18.840
<i>are determined to aim for the goal!</i>

10:18.840 --> 10:20.010
Leave it to me!

10:20.010 --> 10:21.240
You idiots!

10:21.240 --> 10:23.260
Can't you handle such small fry?!

10:24.310 --> 10:25.310
<i>Oh no!</i>

10:25.310 --> 10:29.310
<i>Using Soda's moment of carelessness, Tsubasa sets himself free!</i>

10:29.310 --> 10:31.640
Taki! Tsubasa's unmarked!

10:31.640 --> 10:32.650
We'll join him!

10:32.650 --> 10:33.720
Yeah!

10:34.780 --> 10:35.650
Damn it!

10:36.320 --> 10:40.160
<i>The cross hits a defender and changes course.</i>

10:41.530 --> 10:43.830
<i>Tsubasa turns his back to the goal.</i>

10:43.830 --> 10:47.360
<i>This posture...
He's going for his overhead kick!</i>

10:47.360 --> 10:50.620
<i>This is my first chance. I'll make sure to use it fully!</i>

10:51.380 --> 10:53.040
Like hell I'd let you!

10:53.040 --> 10:57.800
<i>Soda blocks him with a jumping volley!</i>

10:59.260 --> 11:00.510
Nice, Soda!

11:03.650 --> 11:04.310
Got it!

11:04.310 --> 11:07.060
<i>Izawa picks up the loose ball!</i>

11:07.060 --> 11:09.560
Damn it! He's not marked!

11:09.560 --> 11:10.560
Eat this!

11:12.400 --> 11:13.900
Stop him, keeper!

11:15.660 --> 11:17.280
<i>He got it!</i>

11:18.280 --> 11:20.020
<i>A super save!</i>

11:20.020 --> 11:22.390
<i>Nankatsu's barely misses their chance to score!</i>

11:22.390 --> 11:23.950
Nice catch, keeper!

11:23.950 --> 11:28.950
They didn't score, but they have finally made an attack worthy of Nankatsu's name.

11:28.950 --> 11:32.200
Still, Azumaichi MS's defense is really strong.

11:32.200 --> 11:36.460
Seeing that #7 Soda is a defender, one can say that they are a defensive team.

11:36.460 --> 11:39.030
That's right. He's the key.

11:39.030 --> 11:42.580
Blocking Tsubasa's overhead kick is a feat worthy of praise.

11:42.580 --> 11:45.850
Yeah, you're all pretty much right.

11:45.850 --> 11:48.600
Azumaichi is a defensive team.

11:48.600 --> 11:52.050
They conceded no goals in the Osaka Tournament.

11:52.050 --> 11:53.850
And that Makoto Soda...

11:54.920 --> 11:58.610
They call him "Soda the Ace Killer" in Kansai.

11:58.610 --> 12:04.780
He sticks close to his opponent's ace, and stops them by hitting the ball... or their legs.

12:04.780 --> 12:10.640
Our center forward wound up with a leg injury because of his tackles, and was unable to score in the end.

12:10.700 --> 12:11.790
Wha—

12:11.790 --> 12:15.540
Seeing the defensive Azumaichi leading the game by a goal,

12:15.540 --> 12:18.550
I can say that they are sure to win this one.

12:19.360 --> 12:21.340
Soda the Ace Killer...

12:24.090 --> 12:27.350
<i>Damn it! That move earlier...</i>

12:27.350 --> 12:31.920
<u>Because he's being constantly marked, Tsubasa has to cross play.</u>

12:31.920 --> 12:36.610
<i>If Nankatsu loses, it'll be because of Tsubasa's injury.</i>

12:39.940 --> 12:42.490
<i>Nankatsu couldn't score a goal!</i>

12:42.490 --> 12:44.360
<i>The first half ends here.</i>

12:46.240 --> 12:48.130
Well done, boys!

12:48.130 --> 12:52.040
Soda, do you think you can keep marking Tsubasa in the second half too?

12:52.040 --> 12:54.790
If it's hard on you, I can get someone else to help you.

12:54.790 --> 12:58.540
Don't worry. This match is as good as ours.

12:59.550 --> 13:01.920
He injured his leg.

13:01.920 --> 13:03.860
What?!

13:07.920 --> 13:12.930
worst boy's player card

13:13.840 --> 13:16.190
Okawa, what's wrong?

13:16.190 --> 13:18.940
We need you now, come fast.

13:18.940 --> 13:20.440
INFIRMARY

13:22.440 --> 13:24.190
Tsubasa!

13:24.190 --> 13:28.820
That old injury I picked up in the finals against Hyuga is flaring up.

13:28.820 --> 13:32.600
I don't think it's severe, but I need you to tape it.

13:32.600 --> 13:33.700
Quickly, please.

13:33.700 --> 13:35.460
Yes.

13:35.460 --> 13:40.950
Didn't you skip practice during spring of the 2nd year because of this injury?

13:40.950 --> 13:45.340
Yeah. I got it taped by her then.

13:45.340 --> 13:49.160
Manabu, not a word of this to anyone.

13:49.160 --> 13:52.100
There's still the second half, and I don't want them to worry.

13:52.100 --> 13:54.100
I know.

14:00.810 --> 14:02.610
Yep. It's done.

14:02.610 --> 14:03.440
Thanks.

14:06.720 --> 14:07.970
You'll be okay?

14:07.970 --> 14:10.490
Yeah. I'll win, I promise.

14:13.360 --> 14:14.230
All right!

14:14.230 --> 14:18.480
If Tsubasa Ozora is injured, then we only have to think about those three.

14:18.480 --> 14:20.580
Kisugi, Izawa and Taki.

14:20.580 --> 14:23.460
In front of the goal, go man-to-man no matter what.

14:23.460 --> 14:24.560
Yes, sir!

14:24.560 --> 14:28.580
All right! Keep this up; let's shut out the defending champions, Nankatsu.

14:28.580 --> 14:30.890
If there's a chance, go for a counter.

14:30.890 --> 14:31.720
Yeah!

14:33.220 --> 14:36.200
It's okay. We'll get even in the second half for sure!

14:36.200 --> 14:39.350
That's right. We'll tie and reverse the tables!

14:39.350 --> 14:41.160
Just don't get hasty.

14:41.160 --> 14:43.860
Play like you always do, and you'll win!

14:43.860 --> 14:44.940
Yes, sir!

14:45.410 --> 14:47.380
Where's Tsubasa?

14:49.330 --> 14:50.880
What, were you in the toilet?

14:50.880 --> 14:53.370
Yeah. Now that I'm feeling better...

14:53.370 --> 14:56.020
Let's go everyone! To battle in this second half!

14:56.020 --> 14:57.370
Yeah!

14:59.370 --> 15:01.000
We're counting on you, Nankatsu!

15:01.000 --> 15:02.960
Tie the scores first!

15:02.960 --> 15:06.210
Hooray, hooray, 'ichi MS!

15:06.210 --> 15:08.380
Where did you go, Sanae?

15:08.380 --> 15:09.970
I had a small task to do.

15:10.970 --> 15:12.970
<i>The second half starts!</i>

15:15.980 --> 15:18.390
<i>Nankatsu makes an interception already.</i>

15:18.820 --> 15:20.230
Go, Tsubasa!

15:20.230 --> 15:22.860
<i>But Azumaichi MS don't look flustered.</i>

15:22.860 --> 15:26.570
<i>Rather, if Nankatsu goes too forward here, they may get countered.</i>

15:29.390 --> 15:32.070
<i>Soda is still marking him in the second half!</i>

15:32.070 --> 15:33.820
What's the matter, Tsubasa?

15:33.820 --> 15:36.590
Weren't you gonna weasel out of my mark on you?

15:36.590 --> 15:39.080
I guess you can't run with those legs.

15:39.080 --> 15:41.620
<i>This guy knows about my leg...!</i>

15:41.620 --> 15:44.590
If you're not coming, then I'll go to you!

15:47.130 --> 15:47.980
Tsubasa!

15:47.980 --> 15:50.980
<i>Oh, Nankatsu makes a beautiful one-two pass.</i>

15:50.980 --> 15:51.840
Damn it!

15:51.840 --> 15:55.300
<i>However, Soda is in hot pursuit, marking him once more!</i>

15:55.300 --> 16:00.620
<i>I won't lose him for long. I need to make a pass towards the goal.</i>

16:03.560 --> 16:07.070
<i>Are you guys planning on protecting this one goal, Azumaichi MS?</i>

16:07.070 --> 16:11.570
<i>Tsubasa is unable to pass, and Soda is bearing down on him!</i>

16:11.570 --> 16:14.570
<i>Damn it! Then I'm gonna have to bet on this!</i>

16:14.570 --> 16:18.410
<i>Ah! Tsubasa is getting ready to shoot, even from this far out!</i>

16:18.410 --> 16:19.160
What?!

16:19.160 --> 16:21.850
<i>Roberto, I'm channeling you!</i>

16:21.870 --> 16:23.210
I won't let you!

16:28.710 --> 16:34.510
Drive Shot!

16:34.510 --> 16:36.900
<i>Soda's tackle doesn't make it in time!</i>

16:36.900 --> 16:38.970
<i>Tsubasa takes a long shot!</i>

16:38.970 --> 16:42.480
<i>I didn't make it in time! What a quick shot!</i>

16:43.640 --> 16:48.150
<i>But this one's floated over! It looks like this shot will go over...</i>

16:50.980 --> 16:54.560
<i>Ah! The ball that was supposed to go over suddenly drops down!</i>

16:54.560 --> 16:57.280
<i>There must be a huge amount of forward "drive" spin on it!</i>

16:57.280 --> 16:59.530
<i>Come on, get in!</i>

17:03.910 --> 17:05.040
Keeper!

17:05.040 --> 17:06.170
What?!

17:09.900 --> 17:13.050
<i>It's in! The keeper wasn't able to react!</i>

17:13.050 --> 17:15.180
All ri—

17:15.180 --> 17:21.680
<i>No, it's our mistake! It's landed on the net above the goal. It is not a goal!</i>

17:21.680 --> 17:23.100
Damn!

17:23.100 --> 17:26.020
<i>It was a very close long shot for Tsubasa.</i>

17:26.020 --> 17:27.770
<i>That was powerful!</i>

17:27.770 --> 17:30.230
<i>It went right to the net!</i>

17:30.230 --> 17:33.980
<i>Sorry, Roberto. I still can't make it.</i>

17:33.980 --> 17:37.510
<i>I still haven't been able to master that shot.</i>

17:37.510 --> 17:42.370
<i>Also... the Drive Shot takes a greater toll on my pivot leg than I expected.</i>

17:42.370 --> 17:45.290
<i>I can't use it any more this match.</i>

17:45.290 --> 17:48.040
<i>Damn you! Trying to scare me like that!</i>

17:48.040 --> 17:51.960
<i>A Drive Shot? Even I thought of that.</i>

17:57.260 --> 18:01.400
<i>But adding forward spin to a ball is way too hard.</i>

18:01.400 --> 18:10.380
<i>That's why I left that and instead focused on lateral spin; I worked hard to perfect my Razor Shot.</i>

18:10.380 --> 18:17.530
<i>Even for you, Tsubasa... at our age, a Drive Shot is impossible.</i>

18:17.530 --> 18:20.780
<i>Azumaichi MS starts the match with the ball in their hand</i>

18:20.780 --> 18:23.580
All right! We'll attack if there is a chance!

18:23.580 --> 18:24.540
Come on!

18:26.540 --> 18:30.260
<i>I'm pretty sure you hurt yourself more on that last shot.</i>

18:30.260 --> 18:33.670
<i>You won't escape my mark anymore, Tsubasa Ozora!</i>

18:33.670 --> 18:36.300
<i>It's already seven minutes into the second half.</i>

18:39.300 --> 18:42.300
They're just running their mouths about moving to offense!

18:43.480 --> 18:46.220
We're only moving if there's a chance.

18:47.430 --> 18:48.770
Damn you!

18:48.770 --> 18:51.740
<i>That's right! Try to rile your opponents up.</i>

18:51.740 --> 18:53.910
<i>We're only supposed to be scared of Tsubasa's shots.</i>

18:53.910 --> 18:58.150
<i>If Soda can handle him, we'll win in another 20 minutes or so.</i>

18:58.730 --> 19:00.460
<i>Do not get hasty.</i>

19:00.460 --> 19:04.160
<i>If you do, you'll just wind up back in their pace.</i>

19:04.160 --> 19:06.660
<i>The atmosphere in this match doesn't feel very good.</i>

19:06.660 --> 19:09.210
<i>Tsubasa's being completely marked.</i>

19:09.210 --> 19:11.920
<i>Time is running out.</i>

19:11.920 --> 19:14.800
<i>This might end with an upset, y'know...</i>

19:14.800 --> 19:19.820
<i>Nankatsu, without a chance in the second half, has burned through twenty minutes.</i>

19:19.820 --> 19:21.720
<i>Damn it, there's only ten minutes more.</i>

19:23.840 --> 19:24.470
Damn it!

19:25.490 --> 19:28.520
<i>Izawa slides in to steal the ball!</i>

19:29.910 --> 19:33.860
<i>But Soda's mark on Tsubasa makes it impossible to pass to him.</i>

19:34.860 --> 19:38.610
<i>It's not just because of Soda that he's not able to remove his mark!</i>

19:38.610 --> 19:40.440
<i>Even when there's no time left,</i>

19:40.440 --> 19:43.490
<i>we'll still believe in Tsubasa!</i>

19:44.110 --> 19:47.160
<i>Even with the mark, Nankatsu makes a pass onto Tsubasa!</i>

19:47.990 --> 19:50.540
You can't pull ahead of me Tsubasa!

19:50.540 --> 19:52.790
Catch me if you can, Soda!

19:55.000 --> 19:57.920
<i>Oh, Tsubasa goes right onto an opposing player!</i>

19:58.820 --> 20:00.970
<i>He dodges right before hitting him!</i>

20:01.840 --> 20:02.800
<i>All right!</i>

20:02.800 --> 20:05.680
<i>Nankatsu gets a chance after a long time!</i>

20:05.680 --> 20:09.720
<i>Tsubasa need to make a last pass towards the goal.</i>

20:09.720 --> 20:11.810
Tsubasa, you bastard...!

20:11.810 --> 20:17.070
<i>But in front of the goal, Kisugi, Izawa and Taki are completely marked.</i>

20:18.390 --> 20:21.450
<i>Ah! Nanktasu stilll has an unmarked player!</i>

20:21.450 --> 20:22.320
Nagano!

20:22.320 --> 20:23.700
Come on, Tsubasa!

20:23.700 --> 20:25.660
I'll mark him!

20:25.660 --> 20:29.240
<i>Tsubasa can't pass anywhere under these circumstances!</i>

20:29.240 --> 20:31.170
What are you doing, Tsubasa?

20:31.170 --> 20:33.290
You're free! Just go by yourself!

20:33.290 --> 20:35.290
All right! Right there!

20:35.290 --> 20:37.670
<i>Tsubasa lifts a pass towards the goal!</i>

20:37.670 --> 20:39.700
If it's coming upwards, then it's ours.

20:39.700 --> 20:41.940
Everybody, repel the ball with a header!

20:41.940 --> 20:42.550
Yeah!

20:43.930 --> 20:48.240
<i>Ah! Tsubasa had crossed the ball for the center-back Takasugi!</i>

20:48.240 --> 20:49.180
What!?

20:49.180 --> 20:51.180
<i>Take this!</i>

20:51.180 --> 20:53.560
<i>He makes a header runnning towards the goal!</i>

20:54.860 --> 20:55.760
Ah!

20:55.760 --> 20:59.820
<i>It's in! This time, Nankatsu has really tied the scores!</i>

20:59.820 --> 21:01.570
I did it!

21:01.570 --> 21:04.320
Woah! Nice header, Takasugi!

21:05.520 --> 21:06.870
Nice overlap!

21:07.430 --> 21:10.460
You bastard! You made a goal before I did!

21:10.460 --> 21:12.370
Even if that was supposed to be a joke!

21:12.370 --> 21:17.380
<i>Nankatsu finally scores with Takasugi's ambush!</i>

21:17.380 --> 21:21.550
<i>Tsubasa was very attentive, with noticing Takasugi.</i>

21:21.550 --> 21:22.670
Damn it!

21:22.670 --> 21:25.300
If we're even, then the match is ours!

21:25.300 --> 21:28.750
Tsubasa, is your leg okay?

21:30.000 --> 21:32.430
We center-backs are like goalkeepers,

21:32.430 --> 21:35.390
we look at your movements from the back.

21:36.050 --> 21:40.020
Takasugi! It's okay. No need to worry.

21:40.020 --> 21:41.850
Is that so?

21:41.850 --> 21:46.610
<i>Tsubasa! Is it because of his leg that he didn't go by himself?</i>

21:46.610 --> 21:49.870
Phew! I'm a little relieved seeing that.

21:49.870 --> 21:52.330
Nankatsu will go on a roll after this.

21:52.330 --> 21:54.160
That's right.

21:54.160 --> 21:56.140
Damn it! It's even now.

21:56.140 --> 21:58.120
We just needed to go for it a little more.

21:58.120 --> 22:01.040
I got played by you, Tsubasa Ozora.

22:01.720 --> 22:03.760
Don't you guys worry!

22:03.760 --> 22:06.840
I'll get that back with my Razor Shot.

22:07.270 --> 22:12.140
But Soda, this time they'll come prepared for it.

22:12.140 --> 22:17.100
That's okay, my Razor Shot can be used in both ways!

22:38.670 --> 22:44.710
<i>chotto are mi na ace ga tooru</i>

22:38.670 --> 22:44.710
<i>Hey, look over there at the ace passing through</i>

22:44.710 --> 22:50.720
<i>suguremono zo to machijû sawagu</i>

22:44.710 --> 22:50.720
<i>He's the best, and the whole town cheers him on</i>

22:50.720 --> 22:56.770
<i>chô-chô samba, zigzag samba</i>

22:50.720 --> 22:56.770
<i>Butterfly samba, zig-zag samba</i>

22:56.770 --> 23:01.400
<i>aitsu no uwasa de chamba mo hashiru</i>

22:56.770 --> 23:01.400
<i>Even little old ladies go around talking about him</i>

23:03.020 --> 23:07.690
<i>sore ni tsukete mo ore-tacha nan na no</i>

23:03.020 --> 23:07.690
<i>So, even if we have him, who are we?</i>

23:09.030 --> 23:15.120
<i>ball hitotsu ni kiri-kiri mai sa</i>

23:09.030 --> 23:15.120
<i>The ball spins round and round</i>

23:15.120 --> 23:21.170
<i>Dash, dash, dash! Kick and dash!</i>

23:21.170 --> 23:25.630
<i>itsuka kimeru ze inazuma shoot</i>

23:21.170 --> 23:25.630
<i>One day, I'll score with a lightning shot!</i>

23:26.920 --> 23:33.260
<i>son toki ore ga super hero sa</i>

23:26.920 --> 23:33.260
<i>When that happens, I'll become a super hero!</i>

23:33.260 --> 23:39.310
<i>Dash, dash, dash! Kick and dash!</i>

23:39.310 --> 23:45.610
<i>moete seishun kakenukero</i>

23:39.310 --> 23:45.610
<i>This fierce youth is on the field!</i>

23:49.900 --> 24:00.460
COMING UP, EPISODE 36:
RESOLUTION OF EACH
